      "parameters": {
        "width": 488,
        "height": 648,
        "content": "## Draft a community announcement with Gemini, approve in Slack, post to Discord\n\n### How it works\nAutomating social posts is risky if nothing checks them first, so this template keeps a human in the loop. Describe an update in the built-in form and pick a tone, and a Basic LLM Chain with Google Gemini drafts a short, on-brand Discord announcement. Instead of posting it, the Slack node shows the draft with Post it / Discard buttons and pauses the workflow until someone decides. If approved, the post is sent to your Discord channel via its webhook and logged as Posted; if discarded, nothing is published and it is logged as Discarded. A failed Discord post is reported back to Slack so it never fails silently.\n\n### Setup\n1. Connect Google Gemini (PaLM) API, Slack and Google Sheets.\n2. In Post to Discord, paste your Discord channel webhook URL.\n3. Pick the Slack approval channel and point the log at your sheet.\n\n### Customization tips\nSwap Discord for a Telegram channel or an X post, or add scheduling."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
